On Jan 9, 12:42 am, Eric Miears <ewmie...@gmail.com> wrote:
> How do the seasoned hackers handle this situation?

Ranged attacks.  In order to bisect you, in addition to
turning the RNG against you, he also has to be located
adjacent to you, in order to engage you in melee.  If you
can prevent him from being adjacent to you, the chance of
bisection is zero.  Note, however, that as a quest nemesis
he has the innate ability to warp.  (Being fundamentally
unfair is one of the very few ways in which NetHack is like
real life.)

The wiki recommends hitting him with an attack wand first
thing, and when he flees you pick up the tsurugi and
immediately put it into a container.  Another possibility
is to polyself into something non-bisectable.  Personally,
I'd probably combine these two techniques, just to be safe,
because I really *really* don't trust the RNG.


